{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PS3 pushed (change 1796): closed a correctness seam operator review found in PS2's verdict cache.\n\nThe seam: scoped_content_fingerprint resolved blobs at hard-literal HEAD:<path> (health probe HEAD^{tree}). But a --ref <sha>-targeted close (bug 80af, stacked-story flow: transition_close.py resolves the SAME ref for drift checks and threads ref into the completion precheck/verify) verifies and signs against THAT ref's tree — so verdicts proven against the story's tree would have been persisted under a fingerprint of the TIP's blobs: the cache would assert \"these blobs <-> PASS\" for blobs the verifier never examined, and a later re-verify at a matching-tip HEAD could seed those verdicts illegitimately.\n\nHow the ref reaches the verify flow: verify_completion (completion.py) resolves the gate handle via gate_source.resolve_gate_handle(ref, ...) whose SnapshotHandle.sha is the pinned resolved commit (annotate_result stamps it as verified_at_sha). PS3 threads handle.sha as a new verify_ref kwarg: verify_completion -> _verify_completion_inner -> gate_dispatch.produce_completion_verdict -> CompletionAgentStep(verify_ref=...) -> the cache calls.\n\nCache surface changes (completion_verdict_cache.py): scoped_content_fingerprint/load_valid_pass_entries/seed_bank_from_cache/persist_pass_verdicts gain kw-only ref=None (None -> \"HEAD\", byte-compatible default); specs become <ref>:<path> and <ref>^{tree} — the rev-parse subcommand stays literal so the raw-git gate stays green. Persist fingerprints at the ref the verdicts were proven against; load/seed fingerprint at the CURRENT run's verification target. Each entry additionally records verified_ref_sha (resolved commit sha) — informational audit stamp only, never a validity key (keying on it would kill reuse across unrelated commits).\n\nTests (RED-first, all in test_completion_verdict_cache.py, now 21 tests): test_persist_under_ref_binds_the_refs_blobs_not_heads (impact file differs between ref and HEAD -> entry fingerprint matches recompute at ref, not HEAD; verified_ref_sha == ref sha), test_ref_bound_entry_does_not_seed_at_a_differing_head (no load/seed at HEAD; loads AND seeds at the matching ref), test_default_ref_is_head_byte_compatible.\n\nMutation pass on the ref logic: 5 mutants (fingerprint ignores ref; persist drops ref pass-through; load's fingerprint drops ref; verified_ref_sha resolved at HEAD; seed drops ref pass-through) — 5/5 killed (the seed pass-through mutant initially survived; killed by extending the seeding assertions).\n\nGates: check_raw_git_writes rc=0, make lint clean (complexity ratchet new=0/increased=0), make typecheck clean (543 files), targeted suites 86/86 (cache 21, banking, budget contracts, review-output-budget). Module caps respected: completion.py 800, completion_recovery.py 799 (comment trims offset the threading lines)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786753286951674001,"uuid":"4bbfdccd-b22a-4ab2-9a18-8b65b86315ef"}